# name|tier|timeout seconds|command (run from the repo root)|needs|serial
# serial (optional 6th field): the test needs sequential order (shared port / file / state): run.sh runs it alone, after all parallel tests. Everything else runs in parallel; none is marked serial today.
# tier fast = seconds, run on every change that touches the area; slow = run when you touched what it covers (tests/covers.map) and before release.
# findrep_full = 2700+ operations on the C engine and the Python twin (about 3 min); findrep = the quick version
# needs: node | python3 | fileapi (the ../fileapi repo) - when missing the test is reported as SKIP (never as a pass).
lint_waits|fast|20|bash tests/lint_waits.sh|
regex_portability|fast|30|bash tests/regex_portability.sh|
cmd_drift|fast|90|bash tests/cmd_drift.sh|
